{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/contiguousarray\/capacity"]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"capacity"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","title":"capacity","platforms":[{"unavailable":false,"name":"iOS","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"8.0"},{"unavailable":false,"name":"iPadOS","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"8.0"},{"unavailable":false,"name":"Mac Catalyst","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"13.0"},{"unavailable":false,"name":"macOS","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"10.10"},{"unavailable":false,"name":"tvOS","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"9.0"},{"unavailable":false,"name":"visionOS","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"1.0"},{"unavailable":false,"name":"watchOS","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"2.0"}],"modules":[{"name":"Swift"}],"extendedModule":"Swift","externalID":"s:s15ContiguousArrayV8capacitySivp","symbolKind":"property"},"abstract":[{"text":"The total number of elements that the array can contain without","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"allocating new storage.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"capacity","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Int"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every array reserves a specific amount of memory to hold its contents."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"When you add elements to an array and that array begins to exceed its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reserved capacity, the array allocates a larger region of memory and"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"copies its elements into the new storage. The new storage is a multiple"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"of the old storage’s size. This exponential growth strategy means that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"appending an element happens in constant time, averaging the performance"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of many append operations. Append operations that trigger reallocation","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"have a performance cost, but they occur less and less often as the array"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"grows larger."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following example creates an array of integers from an array literal,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"then appends the elements of another collection. Before appending, the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array allocates new storage that is large enough store the resulting"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var numbers = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]","\/\/ numbers.count == 5","\/\/ numbers.capacity == 5","","numbers.append(contentsOf: stride(from: 60, through: 100, by: 10))","\/\/ numbers.count == 10","\/\/ numbers.capacity == 10"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/ContiguousArray\/capacity","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","do